-- title:
--   Igusa level field as a degree (q-1)/2 Kummer extension
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $5 \le q$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$, viewed in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, lies in the nonunits of $A$; write $\kappa$ for the residue field of $A$. Inside the Laurent series field over $\kappa$ consider $E_0 =$ `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,M'$, the $\kappa$-subfield generated by `jqModC` and its $M'$-th expansion `jqNModC`, and the element $\bar g = \bar E_4\bar E_6/\bar\Delta$ obtained as the product of the reductions (via `intSeriesC`) of the integral power series $1 + \sum_{n>0}240\sigma_3(n)X^n$ and $1 - \sum_{n>0}504\sigma_5(n)X^n$, divided by the reduction of $X\cdot$`dedekindEtaUnit` $= X\prod_{n\ge 1}(1-X^n)^{24}$. The assertion has three parts: (i) $\bar g$ is a Kummer generator of exponent $(q-1)/2$ over $E_0$, that is $0 < (q-1)/2$, $\bar g \ne 0$ and $\bar g^{(q-1)/2} \in E_0$; (ii) the field $\kappa$-generated by $E_0 \cup \{\bar g\}$ equals `xHFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,(q^2M')$ `(levelH q M')`, the field generated by reductions of ratios of integral $q$-expansions of equal weight on $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$; and (iii) the relative degree `relfinrank` of that field over $E_0$ is $(q-1)/2$. Here $(q-1)/2$ is natural-number division.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$q$ Igusa picture of the full-level modular curve: the reduced $q$-expansion field at level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, $H$ the principal congruence kernel modulo $q$, is the Kummer extension of $\kappa(X_0(M'))$ generated by $\bar E_4\bar E_6/\bar\Delta$, of degree $(q-1)/2$. It is used in the identification of places, of rings of integers and of Gauss prolongations for the full-level component field over $A$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_isKummerGenerator_eisensteinRatio_and_igusaFunctionField_eq_xHFunctionFieldC_levelH.lean

